  "title": "Chapter 34: Natural Vegetation of India",
  "order": 220,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lm26ud7",
      "content": "Natural vegetation refers to plant communities that grow naturally without human intervention and have been left undisturbed for a long time. India possesses a rich variety of natural vegetation due to variations in relief, soil, temperature and rainfall. "
    },
