    {
      "id": "2hys8w9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Factors Affecting Natural Vegetation"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Natural vegetation in India is primarily determined by climate, rainfall distribution, temperature, and relief features.",
        "Tropical Deciduous Forests represent the most widespread vegetation type across the Indian subcontinent.",
        "Tropical Evergreen Forests occur in high-rainfall regions and maintain dense foliage throughout the year.",
        "Montane Forests display distinct altitudinal zonation corresponding to variations in temperature and elevation.",
        "Mangrove Forests occupy tidal coastal regions and provide vital protection against erosion and storm surges."
      ],
      "id": "mc17yrg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vvl7qwk",
      "content": "The distribution of natural vegetation in India depends on climatic and geographical factors."
    },
