    {
      "id": "8u9dfbr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Major Types of Natural Vegetation in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9ofj95d",
      "content": "Based on temperature and rainfall, Indian vegetation is classified into five major types: Tropical Evergreen Forests, Tropical Deciduous Forests, Thorn Forests, Montane Forests, and Mangrove Forests."
    },
