    {
      "id": "gtsbm7v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Tropical Evergreen Forests – Detailed"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bx78b0r",
      "content": "These forests grow in areas receiving heavy rainfall and high temperature throughout the year. Trees can reach heights of 60 meters or more. The forests are so dense that sunlight rarely reaches the ground."
    },
    {
      "id": "qr0u791",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Tropical Deciduous Forests – Most Important"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8j3dgdq",
      "content": "These are the most widespread forests in India and are economically valuable. They are also called monsoon forests because their growth is closely linked with seasonal rainfall."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2zs3v4t",
      "content": "They are further divided into Moist Deciduous (higher rainfall) and Dry Deciduous (lower rainfall)."
    },
    {
